          "artDescription": "Standalone vertical game artwork for Time-Block Hero, portrait 5:8 composition, Legendary derivative minion. Preserve the established intimate low three-quarter composition of Rift-Reborn Drake: a lost sixteen-to-seventeen-year-old boy fills the upper portrait, looking down in bewildered fear at his own raised hand and ruptured torso inside a damaged frontier-vessel corridor. Retain his youthful angular face, tousled ash-brown hair, gray-green deep-set eyes, slim adolescent frame, deep forest-green expedition-captain coat, dark oxblood-red lining, high collar, map-case straps, and worn brass-like fasteners. Keep the same dramatic foreshortening, recognizable facial identity, hand positions, corridor background, and close-to-medium framing; do not use a distant long shot.\n\nAdd severe but identity-preserving Hollow-Null contradiction. A perfectly lightless causal void has removed part of one cheek, the edge of the nose, and the lower rim of one eye socket; several fragments of the same youthful face occupy slightly incompatible positions, while one intact eye and most of the expression remain recognizable. The facial damage must look like reality missing, not a scar, burn, black makeup, skull exposure, disease, or a clean half-face division. Around the existing missing torso and across both shoulders, arms, waist, and one thigh, show many mutually incompatible material states: wet dark-red biological tissue, pale tendons, displaced ribs and fragments of an older hand; matte cracked ivory ceramic shell plates and splinters; corroded pistons, gears, black cable bundles and ship fasteners; surviving green coat seams and oxblood fabric strips. One biological hand is present while its ceramic forearm lags in another position; a piston joint intersects a living shoulder as both grow and erode; ribs pass through ceramic shell and disconnected fingers skip intermediate motion. Make biological, ceramic, and mechanical fragments visibly distinct and abundant without forming stable cybernetics, armor, or a designed monster anatomy.\n\nUse controlled cold cyan-white edge light to reveal the causal gaps and material differences while keeping his face readable, with charcoal industrial shadows and restrained deep green and oxblood-red accents. Premium industrial sci-fi anime rendering, crisp adolescent facial drawing, hybrid cel-and-painterly surfaces, exceptional Legendary material finish. The causal void must read as absolute missing reality, never black skin, smoke, liquid shadow, or a glowing portal. Avoid a long shot, heroic pose, muscular adult, beard, clean human/monster split, stable biological mutation, tidy cyborg design, generic zombie, readable text, logo, watermark, UI, card frame, decorative border, arrows, cost, or stat icons.",
